(a) Don't use `rw [cast_cast]` — instead use `exact` with a term-level proof: build the eq proof directly: 
```lean
  refine M.spaceFormProjection_covering.monodromy_eq_of_map_eq
      (γ := γloop) (ex := e₁) (ey := e₂) Γ₀ ?_
  dsimp [γloop]
  change Γ₀.map _ = ((Γ₀.map _).cast hx.symm hy.symm).cast hx hy
  rw [Path.Homotopic.Quotient.cast_cast]
  congr 1 <;> exact proof_irrel _ _
```
The `change` replaces `e₁.property` by `hx` — hx : p e₁.1 = q₀ elaborated at the equality type directly. Then rw [cast_cast] sees `cast hx hy` with clean equality-typed args. The change itself might hit the same transparency issue — the goal has e₁.property at the `∈` type and hx at `=` type — they're defeq at default transparency (the `change` tactic uses default transparency? I believe change/convert use semireducible or default). Let me try.

